1. A valid email address must contain a username followed by the "@" symbol and a domain name.
2. The username can contain alphanumeric characters, periods, hyphens, and underscores.
3. The domain name can contain alphanumeric characters and periods.
4. The domain name must have at least one period.
5. The email address must not contain any additional characters or spaces.
6. The email address must not exceed a length of 255 characters.
7. The program should return 1 if the given string is a valid email address, and 0 otherwise.

Reference code:

```perl
sub is_valid_email_address {
  my $email_address = shift;

  if ($email_address =~ /^(?!.*[^A-Za-z0-9\.\-\_@])(?=(?:[A-Za-z0-9\.\-\_]+@)[A-Za-z0-9]+(?:\.[A-Za-z0-9]+)+$)[A-Za-z0-9\.\-\_]+@[A-Za-z0-9]+(?:\.[A-Za-z0-9]+)+$/) {
    return 1;
  }
  else {
    return 0;
  }
}

